      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## MOSS-Image Regional LoRA: full pipeline (ahx)\n\nBoxes → image → character masks → redrawn faces and eyes.\n\n**1. Generate.** Draw the boxes in **MOSS-Image Regional LoRA + Layout Prompt (ahx)**. Select a box to edit its caption, label and **LoRA list** (**+ Add LoRA**: the LoRA acts only inside that box). With no box selected, the Canvas panel holds the image size and the whole-image caption.\n\nThe layer panel lists the front box at the top and the background at the bottom (*▲ front*, *▼ back*); drag a row to reorder. Here the café sign is at the bottom, behind the two people.\n\n**Character LoRAs (placeholders):** each character box has a stand-in LoRA, *CHANGE_ME_left_character_lora* and *CHANGE_ME_right_character_lora*. Select the box, click the LoRA's name and pick your own (or remove it with ×): the run stops with a *not found* error until you do. The detailer uses the same LoRAs on that character's face and eyes. If a LoRA has a trigger word, add it to the box's caption and its detail prompts (the LoRA's text-encoder part is not used).\n\n**Size:** the **Resolution Selector** (in *Settings*, at the top) feeds the node's **width_input** / **height_input**, so the Canvas panel shows the size read-only: pick another ratio or megapixel count there, or delete the two links to set the size in the Canvas panel.\n\n**Background** (behind the boxes, a drawing aid only): **Use the last generated image** is ticked in the Canvas panel, so after the first run the image saved by *Save Image* below shows behind the boxes. Untick it to pick a file from ComfyUI's output folder or your computer (folder button), or connect an image to the node's **background** input, for example a *Load Image (from Outputs)* node (linking *Save Image* itself back would be a loop).\n\n**2. Masks.** **MOSS-Image Character Masks (ahx)** finds the person in each `character` box with SAM3 and masks the face and eyes (tick hair, hands or skin too). Every ticked part needs a detail prompt; they are filled in for the two sample boxes.\n\n**3. Detail.** **MOSS-Image Regional Detailer (ahx)** redraws each part with its prompt and the box's LoRAs. Tick `stop_before_detailing` to check the masks first, then untick it and queue again: the image and masks come from the cache. *Save Image* writes the result to ComfyUI's `output/moss-image/` folder. **Compare Images** at the end shows the whole image before and after detailing: drag the slider across it. (To see each part's own before / after, connect the detailer's `passes` output to a *Preview Image*.)\n\n**4. Layout check (muted).** **MOSS-Image Layout Discovery (ahx)** is a setup tool: run it once after a ComfyUI update (see the note next to it). It is muted so it doesn't run on every queue.\n\n**Settings** (the group at the top): **Seed**, **Steps**, **CFG**, **Sampler** and **Scheduler** each feed both the KSampler and the detailer, so the two always sample alike: change them there, not on those nodes. The seed is **fixed**, so queueing again reuses the cached image; set the Seed node's *control after generate* to *randomize* for a new image each time. The detailer's `denoise` stays on the detailer.\n\n## Models\n\nSame files as the official *MOSS-Image* templates. Download each one into the folder shown, inside your ComfyUI folder:\n\n| file | folder | loaded by |\n|---|---|---|\n| [moss_image_sft_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image/resolve/main/diffusion_models/moss_image_sft_int8_convrot.safetensors) | `ComfyUI/models/diffusion_models/` | Load MOSS-Image model |\n| [qwen3.5_9b_w4a8_gptq.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image/resolve/main/text_encoders/qwen3.5_9b_w4a8_gptq.safetensors) | `ComfyUI/models/text_encoders/` | Load MOSS-Image text encoder |\n| [flux2-vae_small.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image/resolve/main/vae/flux2-vae_small.safetensors) | `ComfyUI/models/vae/` | Load MOSS-Image VAE |\n| [sam3.1_multiplex_fp16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/sam3.1/resolve/main/checkpoints/sam3.1_multiplex_fp16.safetensors) | `ComfyUI/models/checkpoints/` | Load SAM3 (Character Masks) |\n\nA subfolder is fine (e.g. `models/diffusion_models/Moss/`): pick the file again in its loader. After adding a file, press **R** in ComfyUI to refresh the model lists.\n\nSampler settings from the official *MOSS-Image: Text to Image (bounding boxes)* template: 25 steps, cfg 2.5, er_sde, simple.\n"
      ],
      "title": "Read me"
    },
